{
  "bridge_text": "寒风吹过，那棵古老树干里的嗡鸣声听起来确实像某种古老的呼唤。莉娜深吸一口气，拨开垂下的枝条，终于看清了树洞里的模样。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "莉娜站在树洞口，心中既害怕又好奇。她裹紧了红色的羊毛大衣，跨过那道被积雪掩埋的门槛，走进了这棵大树的内部。就在那树洞的阴影里，她发现了一圈盘旋向下的楼梯，而在最高的一级台阶上，坐着一只穿着补丁绿马甲的老灰狐狸。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While the fox holds his secrets close, the path down the hollow tree calls to Lina. She stands before Mosk, ready to see what lies at the bottom.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood firm, her eyes meeting the fox’s weary gaze. She knew there was more to this grumpy guardian than his prickly words, but for now, she waited to see if he would truly let her pass or continue to block the way."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said, this is for the trouble of walking me down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk watching her closely and the mystery of the humming still waiting below, Lina stood firm on the top step. She knew the path ahead required courage.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a clawed finger toward the door, his expression stern. Undeterred, Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the final apple of the season. She placed the fruit on the step between them, offering it as a gift for his time. Mosk stared at the apple for a long moment, his stony gaze softening, before he stood up, adjusted his green vest, and silently began to descend the stairs."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the base of the staircase, the humming transformed into a gentle, rhythmic song. A firefly, as large as a robin, rested upon a bed of emerald moss, her golden light flickering and dim. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. He whispered that she had once been his dearest friend, but he had failed to bring her medicine during a harsh winter, and he had been guarding this tree in shame ever since."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
