{
  "bridge_text": "Kindness often finds a way where shadows cannot, and as Mosk turns toward the stairs, we shall see if her gift truly lightens the path ahead.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his golden eyes reflecting its bright red skin. Then he stood up, pulled his vest tight, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. He seemed to carry a heavy weight on his shoulders as he began the slow descent into the hollow's dim, quiet belly."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the firefly resting softly on that damp, velvety bed of moss, the air grew heavy with the weight of old memories. Mosk looked down at his friend, his heart still heavy with the shadows of the past.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming softened into a quiet, mournful song. There, nestled on a thick, velvet-green carpet of moss—the perfect, cool bed for a weary traveler—lay a firefly as large as a robin. Her light flickered, nearly spent. Mosk’s whiskers trembled with sorrow; he whispered that she had once been his dear friend, but he had failed to bring her medicine during a harsh winter long ago. Ever since that cold day, he had guarded this hollow tree, too ashamed to look her in the eye until now."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With that old grey fox watching her from the top step, Lina stood firm, refusing to leave while the secret of the humming remained hidden.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a curl of stairs spiraled downward into the dark. At the very top step sat Mosk, an old grey fox in a patched green vest. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering on stone as he warned Lina that the tree was not for visitors and she should return home to forget the strange humming. But Lina shook her head, insisting that she could not possibly forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

